y also including the myanmar  military  about which china is not really happy  china's interest is not  seeing a military coup being restored in  myanmar  don't forget the chinese government has  also been cooperating with the  democratically elected  government of aung san chuchi quite  intensively indeed china's interest is  not establishing a certain  type of political system in myanmar but  having  an overall political system in place  because  myanmar is a core country in china's  geostrategic interest  it is the transit country between the  indian ocean  and the southwestern chinese province of  yunnan  it could be extremely important as a  transit country should something  like we have seen it happening in the  sewers canal  happened in the very sensitive area of  the malacca strait  in that case china needs stability in  the political system  in order to use myanmar as a transit  corridor  for oil gas resources even for trade  so it's not about the domestic situation  in myanmar  predominantly but certainly about the  geostrategic position of the country  so ultimately it's all about economic  interest is that is that what it is  it is economic interest it is geostating  interest  china has investing been investing  extremely intensively in myanmar in  railways  in streets in pipelines in deep sea  ports  there is also a geostrategic element for  china's  ever stronger navy moving around the  indian ocean  and having deep supports in myanmar  available  so it's a whole spectrum of geostrategic  interests  tell us because you know we we've seen  you know others in the international  community community  condemning the moves by uh the military  in myanmar as the death toll there is  rising  the u.s and the uk have imposed economic  sanctions on the country  um how do you see this now sort of  shaking out going forward because you  know we have some countries that are  trying to put pressure  on the country and then others um  that that that that you know seem 